pages.content:
While `indexOf()` scans from left to right, **`lastIndexOf()`** searches backwards from right to left, returning the starting index of the **last occurrence** of a character or substring.

### Syntax and Practical Applications

```java
int lastIndex = str.lastIndexOf(String substr);
int lastIndexFrom = str.lastIndexOf(String substr, int fromIndex);
```

### Common Real-World Use Case: Extracting File Extensions

```java
public class LastIndexOfDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String path = "/users/ashok/documents/financial_report.2025.final.pdf";

        // Find the last dot to isolate the file extension
        int lastDotIndex = path.lastIndexOf('.');
        if (lastDotIndex != -1) {
            String extension = path.substring(lastDotIndex + 1);
            System.out.println("File Extension: " + extension); // Output: pdf
        }

        // Find the last path separator to extract the filename
        int lastSlashIndex = path.lastIndexOf('/');
        if (lastSlashIndex != -1) {
            String fileName = path.substring(lastSlashIndex + 1);
            System.out.println("Filename: " + fileName); // Output: financial_report.2025.final.pdf
        }
    }
}
```

