codeCard.code:
public class StringManipulationOverview {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String greeting = "  Hello, Java World!  ";

        // 1. Case conversion
        System.out.println("Upper: " + greeting.toUpperCase());
        System.out.println("Lower: " + greeting.toLowerCase());

        // 2. Whitespace trimming
        String trimmed = greeting.trim();
        System.out.println("Trimmed: '" + trimmed + "'");

        // 3. Character & substring replacement
        System.out.println("Replaced: " + trimmed.replace("Java", "Modern Java"));

        // 4. Splitting & Joining
        String[] words = trimmed.split(" ");
        System.out.println("Word count: " + words.length);
        String joined = String.join(" | ", words);
        System.out.println("Joined: " + joined);
    }
}

pages.content:
The `toUpperCase()` method in Java is used to convert **all the characters in a string to uppercase**. This method is useful for formatting text, standardizing input, and making case-insensitive comparisons.

**Syntax:**
```java
String upperString = originalString.toUpperCase();
```
---

**Example:**
```java
class Seedit {
 public static void main(String[] args) {
 // Declare and initialize a string
 String originalString = "hello world";

 // Convert the string to uppercase using toUpperCase() method
 String upperString = originalString.toUpperCase();

 // Print the result
 System.out.println("Uppercase Message: " + upperString);
 }
}
```

**Expected Output:**
```default
Uppercase Message: HELLO WORLD
```

codeCard.code:
public class UpperCaseDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String title = "mastering java strings";

        // Calling toUpperCase() returns a new string
        String upperTitle = title.toUpperCase();

        System.out.println("Original: " + title);      // mastering java strings
        System.out.println("Uppercase: " + upperTitle); // MASTERING JAVA STRINGS

        // Non-alphabetic characters remain unchanged
        String code = "java-21_v2.0";
        System.out.println("Code: " + code.toUpperCase()); // JAVA-21_V2.0
    }
}

