### Independent Practice Checkpoint: String Operations Part-1

Put your knowledge to the test by solving practical string processing challenges.

#### Challenge 1: Sensitive Data Masking
Write a method that masks all but the last 4 characters of a payment card number with asterisks (`*`):
- Input: `"4532759182341098"`
- Output: `"************1098"`
- Edge case: If length is 4 or less, return the string unmasked.

#### Challenge 2: Count Upper, Lower, and Digit Characters
Traverse a string and tally the count of:
1. Uppercase characters (`Character.isUpperCase(c)`)
2. Lowercase characters (`Character.isLowerCase(c)`)
3. Numeric digits (`Character.isDigit(c)`)

#### Solution Walkthrough:
```java
public class StringPracticePart1 {
    public static String maskCardNumber(String card) {
        if (card == null || card.length() <= 4) return card;
        int maskLength = card.length() - 4;
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
        for (int i = 0; i < maskLength; i++) {
            sb.append('*');
        }
        sb.append(card.substring(maskLength));
        return sb.toString();
    }
}
```

codeCard.code:
public class CardMasker {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String card = "4532759182341098";
        System.out.println("Masked: " + maskCard(card));

        String shortCode = "911";
        System.out.println("Short:  " + maskCard(shortCode));
    }

    public static String maskCard(String cardNumber) {
        if (cardNumber == null || cardNumber.length() <= 4) {
            return cardNumber;
        }
        int maskCount = cardNumber.length() - 4;
        char[] masked = new char[cardNumber.length()];
        for (int i = 0; i < maskCount; i++) {
            masked[i] = '*';
        }
        for (int i = maskCount; i < cardNumber.length(); i++) {
            masked[i] = cardNumber.charAt(i);
        }
        return new String(masked);
    }
}

