### Independent Practice Checkpoint: String Operations Part-2

#### Challenge 1: Extract File Extension
Write a robust method that extracts the file extension from a file path:
- Input: `"images/profiles/avatar.png"` -> Output: `"png"`
- Input: `"archive.tar.gz"` -> Output: `"gz"`
- Input: `"Makefile"` -> Output: `""` (no extension)
- Input: `".gitignore"` -> Output: `""` (hidden file without extension)

#### Challenge 2: Title-Case Every Word
Given an arbitrary sentence, capitalize the first letter of every word while making the remaining characters lowercase.
- Input: `"wELcOmE tO jAvA pROgRAmMiNg"`
- Output: `"Welcome To Java Programming"`

#### Solution Walkthrough:
```java
public class StringPracticePart2 {
    public static String getFileExtension(String path) {
        if (path == null) return "";
        int lastSlash = Math.max(path.lastIndexOf('/'), path.lastIndexOf('\\'));
        String filename = (lastSlash != -1) ? path.substring(lastSlash + 1) : path;
        int lastDot = filename.lastIndexOf('.');
        if (lastDot <= 0 || lastDot == filename.length() - 1) {
            return "";
        }
        return filename.substring(lastDot + 1);
    }
}
```

codeCard.code:
public class FileExtensionExtractor {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String[] files = {"report.pdf", "archive.tar.gz", "README", ".bashrc", "image.JPEG"};
        for (String f : files) {
            System.out.printf("%-15s -> extension: '%s'%n", f, getExtension(f));
        }
    }

    public static String getExtension(String filename) {
        if (filename == null) return "";
        int dot = filename.lastIndexOf('.');
        // Check that dot exists and is not the very first or very last char
        if (dot <= 0 || dot == filename.length() - 1) {
            return "";
        }
        return filename.substring(dot + 1).toLowerCase();
    }
}

